  "specs/001-ledgerline-inventory-3-1-clone/spec.md": "# Feature Specification: Ledgerline Inventory 3.1 clone\n\n**Feature Branch**: `001-ledgerline-inventory-3-1-clone`\n**Created**: 2026-11-07\n**Status**: Draft\n**Input**: Recorded with Retrace: 2 workflow(s), 5 step(s), 5 API operation(s). Every statement below cites recorded evidence (`evidence/`); nothing is invented.\n\n## User Scenarios & Testing *(mandatory)*\n\n### User Story 1 - Main Menu to Adjust Stock (Priority: P1)\n\nRecorded steps: open Inventory → open item WID-0042 → click Adjust Stock…. Screens seen: Main Menu, Inventory, Item Detail, Adjust Stock.\n\n**Why this priority**: Recorded workflow 1; priorities follow recording order. [NEEDS CLARIFICATION: confirm priority]\n\n**Independent Test**: `evals/playwright/s7c1e4a90.spec.ts` replays the 3 recorded step(s).\n\n**Acceptance Scenarios**:\n\n1. **Given** the user is on “Main Menu”, **When** they open Inventory, **Then** “Inventory” is shown. ([reference](../../reference/screens/s7c1e4a90-5d2c91a7-e04b-4f63-8a1d-7b3e6c0f9152.png))\n   - Likely calls (timing only): `GET /api/items`\n2. **Given** the user is on “Inventory”, **When** they open item WID-0042, **Then** “Item Detail” is shown. ([reference](../../reference/screens/s7c1e4a90-b84e0d3f-29c6-4a17-95e2-c1f7a3d60b48.png))\n   - Likely calls (timing only): `GET /api/items/{itemId}`\n3. **Given** the user is on “Item Detail”, **When** they click Adjust Stock…, **Then** “Adjust Stock” is shown. ([reference](../../reference/screens/s7c1e4a90-3a7f5c09-d1b2-4e86-a3c4-8f0b2e9d7165.png))\n\n---\n\n### User Story 2 - Orders to Supplier Card (Priority: P2)\n\nRecorded steps: open order PO-10482 → open supplier Acme Fasteners. Screens seen: Orders, Order PO-10482, Supplier Card.\n\n**Why this priority**: Recorded workflow 2; priorities follow recording order. [NEEDS CLARIFICATION: confirm priority]\n\n**Independent Test**: `evals/playwright/s9b2f07d3.spec.ts` replays the 2 recorded step(s).\n\n**Acceptance Scenarios**:\n\n1. **Given** the user is on “Orders”, **When** they open order PO-10482, **Then** “Order PO-10482” is shown. ([reference](../../reference/screens/s9b2f07d3-71b9d3e5-08a4-4c2f-b6e1-9d3a5f7c0824.png))\n   - Likely calls (timing only): `GET /api/orders/{orderId}`\n2. **Given** the user is on “Order PO-10482”, **When** they open supplier Acme Fasteners, **Then** “Supplier Card” is shown. ([reference](../../reference/screens/s9b2f07d3-2e8c4f61-a7d9-4b35-9c02-6f1e8b3d4a97.png))\n   - Likely calls (timing only): `GET /api/suppliers/{supplierId}`\n\n---\n\n### Edge Cases\n\n- Recording gap: Adjust Stock was opened but not submitted because saving writes stock levels. What should happen here? [NEEDS CLARIFICATION]\n- Recording gap: Reports and the Suppliers list were not explored in this scan. What should happen here? [NEEDS CLARIFICATION]\n- What happens when a list or view is empty? (Not recorded.)\n- How does the app handle a failed or slow API call? (Not recorded.)\n\n## Requirements *(mandatory)*\n\n### Functional Requirements\n\n- **FR-001**: System MUST provide the “Main Menu” view ([reference](../../reference/screens/s7c1e4a90-0f4b8e21-7c3a-4d59-b1e6-2a9d5c7f0384.png)).\n- **FR-002**: System MUST provide the “Inventory” view ([reference](../../reference/screens/s7c1e4a90-5d2c91a7-e04b-4f63-8a1d-7b3e6c0f9152.png)).\n- **FR-003**: System MUST provide the “Item Detail” view ([reference](../../reference/screens/s7c1e4a90-b84e0d3f-29c6-4a17-95e2-c1f7a3d60b48.png)).\n- **FR-004**: System MUST provide the “Adjust Stock” view ([reference](../../reference/screens/s7c1e4a90-3a7f5c09-d1b2-4e86-a3c4-8f0b2e9d7165.png)).\n- **FR-005**: System MUST provide the “Orders” view ([reference](../../reference/screens/s9b2f07d3-c6e2a8d4-f913-4b07-8d5a-1e4c9b7f2036.png)).\n- **FR-006**: System MUST provide the “Order PO-10482” view ([reference](../../reference/screens/s9b2f07d3-71b9d3e5-08a4-4c2f-b6e1-9d3a5f7c0824.png)).\n- **FR-007**: System MUST provide the “Supplier Card” view ([reference](../../reference/screens/s9b2f07d3-2e8c4f61-a7d9-4b35-9c02-6f1e8b3d4a97.png)).\n- **FR-008**: Users MUST be able to open Inventory (from “Main Menu”).\n- **FR-009**: Users MUST be able to open item WID-0042 (from “Inventory”).\n- **FR-010**: Users MUST be able to click Adjust Stock… (from “Item Detail”).\n- **FR-011**: Users MUST be able to open order PO-10482 (from “Orders”).\n- **FR-012**: Users MUST be able to open supplier Acme Fasteners (from “Order PO-10482”).\n- **FR-013**: System MUST implement `GET /api/items` as described by `getApiItems` in `contracts/openapi.json`.\n- **FR-014**: System MUST implement `GET /api/items/{itemId}` as described by `getApiItemsByItemId` in `contracts/openapi.json`.\n- **FR-015**: System MUST implement `GET /api/orders` as described by `getApiOrders` in `contracts/openapi.json`.\n- **FR-016**: System MUST implement `GET /api/orders/{orderId}` as described by `getApiOrdersByOrderId` in `contracts/openapi.json`.\n- **FR-017**: System MUST implement `GET /api/suppliers/{supplierId}` as described by `getApiSuppliersBySupplierId` in `contracts/openapi.json`.\n\n### Key Entities *(include if feature involves data)*\n\n- **Item**: seen in API paths; attributes include `bin`, `description`, `id`, `on_hand`, `reorder_point`, `sku`, `unit_cost`.\n- **Order**: seen in API paths; attributes include `id`, `lines`, `number`, `order_date`, `status`, `supplier_id`, `total`.\n- **Supplier**: seen in API paths; attributes include `id`, `lead_time_days`, `name`, `phone`, `terms`.\n\n## Success Criteria *(mandatory)*\n\n### Measurable Outcomes\n\n- **SC-001**: Every non-held-out scenario in `evals/playwright/` passes against the running clone.\n- **SC-002**: No scenarios are held out (fewer than 3 recorded workflows); record more to measure overfitting.\n- **SC-003**: Every operation in `contracts/openapi.json` is implemented and its responses validate against the inferred schemas.\n- **SC-004**: Each screen matches the layout and content of its reference screenshot in `reference/screens/` when reviewed side by side.\n\n## Assumptions\n\n- Network capture ran; the API calls it saw are in `contracts/openapi.json`.\n- The evidence for Ledgerline Inventory 3.1 was captured on macOS. See `reference/rebuild-profile.json` for the declared SaaS target or captured desktop platform; confirm the clone deployment target.\n- Text the user typed while recording was redacted; tests use placeholder text.\n- API calls are linked to UI steps by timing only (\"likely\"); treat them as hints, not requirements.\n- The clone recreates behaviour and layout; it must not reuse the original's name, logos or other brand assets.\n- Modernization idea (not observed): Type-ahead search in the Inventory grid\n\n## Platform, stack and performance assessment\n\nSee [rebuild profile](../../reference/rebuild-profile.json) for the target platform, legacy-stack evidence and limitations, proposed modern alternatives, performance goals, observed timings and scan coverage. Proposals are not observed facts; unknown internals and partial coverage remain explicit.\n",
